   "+0.6s","event":"page code set the date field to \"01/11/2026\" via setDate ← setDateTimePickerValue ← applyUnavailableDates ← resolveWith ← (XMLHttpRequest.send) ← send ← ajax ← getUnavailableDates ← (setTimeout) ← onMonthChange ← setDate"

 So it seems that after typing the date, there was a setTimeout that triggered a getUnavailableDates via onMonthChange? Why would the month change?

 Actually, note that the user typed the date and pressed Enter. The date input change might have triggered the flatpickr's onChange, which then called getAvailableHours and updateConfirmFrame.
 But then, somehow, a setTimeout (maybe from the onMonthChange handler) ran and changed the date.

